From 53ad48d38c22eb26fc79b13d5f4468e9038b0082 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: evilcomputer12 <martinrobotika@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 01:55:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/22] xgameruntime: Add TokenAndSignature and UserInfo IPC
 messages to the xodus layer.

Protocol (XML over xodus.sock, service replies with type + 1):
- type 5/6 TokenAndSignatureRequest/Response (ClientId, TitleId decimal, Url,
  Method, Headers, Body base64, ForceRefresh -> Token, Signature, Expiry or
  Error/Message, plus the optional identity elements Xuid, Gamertag,
  ModernGamertag, ModernGamertagSuffix, UniqueModernGamertag, AgeGroup, Uhs).
- type 7/8 UserInfoRequest/Response (ClientId, TitleId, ForceRefresh ->
  SignedIn + identity elements, SignedIn=false, or Error/Message).
- XodusMessageType enum mirroring common.proto replaces the literal ids.

Plumbing: ITokenAndSignatureResponse/IUserInfoResponse objects, libxml2
builders/parsers (xmlNewTextChild so URLs with '&' stay valid, no token
or XML content in traces), IXodusService::TokenAndSignatureRequest and
UserInfoRequest with a shared send/receive helper, a per-request timeout
on IIPCLayer::SendRequestAsync.

IPC layer fixes needed for any reply larger than a PONG: replies are
AddRef'd before being handed to the waiting request, requests are
serialised (no correlation id on the wire), the receive buffer grows to a
full 64 KB frame and lives on the heap, timeouts are failures instead of
HRESULT_FROM_NT(STATUS_TIMEOUT), a closed connection wakes the request in
flight, bad magic resets the buffer instead of wedging the reader.

Startup: the socket is no longer connected during XGameRuntimeInitialize.
XodusEnsureService() connects lazily (socket, reader, PING) once, honours
XODUS_OFFLINE=1 and fails quietly so games keep their offline user when
the service is absent. The MessageBox on a refused connect is gone.

IWineAsync: results are owned references (GetResults hands them out,
AsyncInfo releases its copy), the outer operation reference taken by
Start() is released when the callback ends, the callback's PROPVARIANT is
initialised, failed Create paths no longer touch an unset AsyncInfo.

MsaToken path: ClientId element in PascalCase as the service expects, the
body no longer includes the trailing NUL, errors are returned instead of
an unconditional S_OK, and the response XML is no longer traced.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
